# qkt backtest project

This project was generated by `qkt create template --kind backtest`.

It is a research scaffold for running a local backtest from data mounted at
`/data`. It does not configure a live broker.

## First Run

```bash
cp .env.example .env
$EDITOR .env
make backtest
```

## Environment Values

Required:

- `QKT_IMAGE_TAG`: QKT image tag. The generated default pins to the QKT version
  that created this project.
- `BACKTEST_FROM`, `BACKTEST_TO`: backtest window.

Usually tune:

- `QKT_STARTING_BALANCE`: simulated starting capital.

Keep `.env` out of Git.

## Commands

- `make backtest`: run `strategies/backtest.qkt` across the configured window.
- `make shell`: open a shell in the QKT container.

## Data

Put local market data under `data/` using the layout expected by
`qkt.config.yaml`. The generated config uses `source: local` and
`data_root: /data`.

Scaffolded by qkt v{{QKT_VERSION}}.
